# Process Charter: IT Incident Management

## 1. Process Objective
Restore normal IT service operations as quickly as possible following an incident or disruption, minimizing negative impact on business performance.

## 2. Severity & SLA Matrix
| Severity Level | Definition | Response Target | Resolution Target | Escalation Path |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **P1 - Critical** | Core ERP or regional WAN down nationwide | < 15 Mins | < 2 Hours | IT Manager -> Executive Management |
| **P2 - High** | Major branch disruption / key function blocked | < 30 Mins | < 4 Hours | Infrastructure Lead |
| **P3 - Medium** | Partial disruption / workaround available | < 2 Hours | < 8 Hours | Tier 2 Support |
| **P4 - Low** | Individual / minor issue | < 4 Hours | < 24 Hours | Tier 1 Service Desk |

## 3. Workflow Steps
1. **Identification & Logging:** Ticket created in ServiceNow.
2. **Categorization & Prioritization:** Severity assigned (P1 - P4).
3. **Diagnosis & Investigation:** Initial analysis by Tier 1 / Tier 2.
4. **Resolution & Recovery:** Application of fix or workaround.
5. **Closure:** User verification and ticket closure.
